   "id": "pmt/pure-core-1/ch5/q1",
   "question": "<p>Diagrams not drawn to scale</p><figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:95mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/pmt/pure-core-1-ch5/q01-fig-1.png\" alt=\"Figure 1: cross-section AOBCD of a bird bath: vertical sides AD and BC of height 1.16 m, base AB of width 0.4 m with O its midpoint, and a curved bowl CD between the tops of the sides. Figure 2: the curve CD on x and y axes, symmetric about the y-axis, between x = -0.2 and x = 0.2, with dashed vertical lines from D and C down to the x-axis\"></figure><p>Figure 1 shows the central cross-section <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AOBCD\"></span> of a circular bird bath, which is made of concrete. Measurements of the height and diameter of the bird bath, and the depth of the bowl of the bird bath have been taken in order to estimate the amount of concrete that was required to make this bird bath.</p><p>Using these measurements, the cross-sectional curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"CD\"></span>, shown in Figure 2, is modelled as a curve with equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=1+kx^2\\qquad-0.2\\leqslant x\\leqslant0.2\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span> is a constant and where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"O\"></span> is the fixed origin.</p><p>The height of the bird bath measured 1.16 m and the diameter, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AB\"></span>, of the base of the bird bath measured 0.40 m, as shown in Figure 1.</p><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\"><li>Suggest the maximum depth of the bird bath. <span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></li><li>Find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span>. <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li><li>Hence find the volume of concrete that was required to make the bird bath according to this model. Give your answer, in <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm m^3\"></span>, correct to 3 significant figures. <span class=\"marks\">(7)</span></li><li>State a limitation of the model. <span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></li></ol><p>It was later discovered that the volume of concrete used to make the bird bath was <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0.127\\ \\mathrm m^3\"></span> correct to 3 significant figures.</p><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\" start=\"5\"><li>Using this information and the answer to part (c), evaluate the model, explaining your reasoning. <span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></li></ol>",
